# What NOT to upload when `gcloud run deploy --source .` builds the image.
#
# Without this file gcloud falls back to .gitignore, which is a different
# question entirely: .gitignore is about what not to commit, not about what
# the build needs. The Dockerfile then does its own filtering via
# .dockerignore, so keep the two in step.
#
# .git is the big one. It carries every version of a repo whose history
# includes multi-megabyte drawings, and none of it reaches the image.
.git
.gitignore
.github

.venv
.venv-test
__pycache__/
*.pyc
.pytest_cache

# Docs and deployment blueprints for other hosts. The container never reads
# them, and leaving them out keeps each deploy's upload small.
docs
DEPLOY.md
RENDER.md
CLOUDRUN.md
README.md
render.yaml
fly.toml
Procfile
requirements-dev.txt

tests

# deploy/cloudrun.env.yaml is read by gcloud on this machine, before
# anything is uploaded, so excluding `deploy/` here would not break it. It
# stays out of the image instead, via .dockerignore, where it belongs.
deploy
